1
00:00:00,077 --> 00:00:02,330
(Q1) Hello, West Bay Hotel. Can I help you?

2
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:06,656
Oh, good morning. I'm ringing about your advertisement in the Evening Gazette.

3
00:00:06,656 --> 00:00:09,540
Is that the one for temporary staff?

4
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:10,791
That's right.

5
00:00:10,791 --> 00:00:17,942
Yes. I'm afraid the person who's dealing with that isn't in today, but can give you the main details if you like.

6
00:00:17,942 --> 00:00:22,243
[🟢 staff you are looking for = vacancy] Yes please. Could you tell me what kind of staff you are looking for?

7
00:00:22,243 --> 00:00:24,772
[Q1答案句] We're looking for waiters at the moment.

8
00:00:24,772 --> 00:00:28,362
[⭕️干扰项] There was one post for a cook, but that's already been taken.

9
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:32,023
(Q2) Oh right. Erm, what are the hours of work?

10
00:00:32,023 --> 00:00:40,298
There are two different shifts - there's a day shift from 7 to 2 and a late shift from 4 till 11.

11
00:00:40,298 --> 00:00:43,029
[🟢 定位词 choose] And can people choose which one they want to do?

12
00:00:43,029 --> 00:00:46,921
Not normally, because everyone would choose the day shift I suppose.

13
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:49,203
You alternate from one week to another.

14
00:00:49,203 --> 00:00:53,797
Okay. I'm just writing all this down. What about time off?

15
00:00:53,797 --> 00:01:00,366
[Q2答案句] You get one day off and I think you can negotiate which one you want, it's more or less up to you.

16
00:01:00,366 --> 00:01:03,650
But it has to be the same one every week.

17
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:05,474
(Q3) Do you know what the rates of pay are?

18
00:01:05,474 --> 00:01:13,625
[Q3答案句] Yes, I've got them here, You get ￡5.50 an hour, and that includes a break.

19
00:01:13,625 --> 00:01:15,812
(Q4) Do I have to go home to eat or...

20
00:01:15,812 --> 00:01:22,274
[Q4答案句] You don't have to. You can get a meal in the hotel if you want to, and there's no charge for it so you might as well.

21
00:01:22,274 --> 00:01:30,168
(Q5) Oh good. Yes, so let's see. I'd get er, two hundred and twenty one, no,two hundred and thirty one pounds a week?

22
00:01:30,168 --> 00:01:35,701
You'd also get tips - our guests tend to be quite generous.

23
00:01:35,701 --> 00:01:39,224
[🟢提示进题] Erm, is there a uniform? What about clothes?

24
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:45,660
[Q5答案句] Yes, I forgot to mention that. You need to wear a white shirt, just a plain one, and dark trousers.

25
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:49,785
You know, not green or anything like that. And we don't supply those.

26
00:01:49,785 --> 00:01:53,509
(Q6) That's okay, I've got trousers, I'd just have to buy a couple of shirts.

27
00:01:53,509 --> 00:01:56,436
What about anything else? Do I need a waistcoat or anything?

28
00:01:56,436 --> 00:01:59,540
[Q6答案句， lend you = supplied] You have to wear a jacket, but the hotel lends you that.

29
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:04,257
(Q7) I see. Er, one last thing - I don't know what the starting date is.

30
00:02:04,257 --> 00:02:12,512
[Q7答案句] Just a minute, I think it's some time around the end of June. Yes, the 28th, in time for the summer.

31
00:02:12,512 --> 00:02:14,834
[⭕️干扰项] That's great. I'm available from the 10th.

32
00:02:14,834 --> 00:02:20,253
(Q8) Oh good. Well, if you can call again you need to speak to the Service Manager.

33
00:02:20,253 --> 00:02:28,297
[Q8答案句] Her name's Jane Urwin, that's U-R-W-I-N, and she'll probably arrange to meet you.

34
00:02:28,297 --> 00:02:31,454
(Q9) Okay. And when's the best time to ring?

35
00:02:31,454 --> 00:02:40,987
[Q9答案句] Could you call tomorrow? Um, she usually starts checking the rooms at midday, so before then if you can, so she'll have more time to chat.

36
00:02:40,987 --> 00:02:43,916
(Q10) I'll just give you her number because she's got a direct line.

37
00:02:43,916 --> 00:02:44,832
Thanks.

38
00:02:44,832 --> 00:02:48,728
It's 832 double-0 9.

39
00:02:48,728 --> 00:02:51,065
823 double-0 9?&nbsp;

40
00:02:51,065 --> 00:02:53,736
832.&nbsp;

41
00:02:53,736 --> 00:02:55,969
Oh, okay. Yes, I'll do that.

42
00:02:55,969 --> 00:03:00,835
[Q10答案句 🟢 10定位] And by the way, she will ask you for a reference, so you might like to be thinking about that.

43
00:03:00,835 --> 00:03:03,969
You know, just someone who knows you and can vouch for you.

44
00:03:03,969 --> 00:03:07,065
Yes, no problem. Well, thanks very much for your help.

45
00:03:07,065 --> 00:03:07,804
You're welcome. Bye.

46
00:03:07,804 --> 00:03:10,304
Bye.

